  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:food-safety-blockchain",
  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "Food Safety Blockchain is the application of distributed ledger technology to establish immutable, multi-party farm-to-fork audit trails that enable near-instantaneous contamination source identification and surgical product recalls. By recording each Critical Tracking Event\u2014harvest, cooling, packing, shipment, receipt\u2014as a cryptographically linked on-chain entry, the approach reduces trace-back from days to seconds, minimises the volume of food unnecessarily recalled, and provides regulators and consumers with verifiable provenance data.",
